{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1152644-life-is-strange-a-disguised-mage-the-awakening-story","id":1152644,"title":"Life is Strange: a disguised Mage The Awakening story?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-24T17:16:39-07:00","id":1152644,"title":"Life is Strange: a disguised Mage The Awakening story?","content":"Okay, okay, the topic might make absolutely no sense to many of you but something I've noticed has blown my mind. In this forum there's another topic about characters from pop culture and how they fit in the CofD universe, a user said that Life is Strange could be seen as an Acanthus Awakening, and you know what? THAT MAKES SO MUCH SENSE.<br /> <br /> I'm going to try to avoid spoilers to the best of my ability but if you haven't played the game yet please don't read.<br /> <br /> The starting scene with Max's vision of the storm approaching Arcadia Bay could easily be seen as her first journey to the supernal realm, the name &quot;Arcadia Bay&quot; itself says it all. Next scene she wakes up in class, appearing to not have slept at Jefferson's lecture. Later, the picture of the butterfly she took in the toilets could symbolize her mark on the Supernal, now she's a Mage though unaware of the fact. When the accident happened, Max instinctively used improvised magic with the Time Arcana to save Chloe's life, rewinding time back to class. Even though this seems like a great feat for a newly Awakened Mage, I like to think that when they are under stress they can perform magic they normally couldn't do (which explains why she wouldn't be able to do something like that later in the game)<br /> <br /> Later in the game you can see that abuse of her powers strain her, she causes paradoxes ripping reality apart, intruding abyssal energies into the world. Though why telling Chloe about magic didn't cause a paradox? Chloe Price is a Sleepwalker!<br /> <br /> I'm not going to share spoilers but you can see later how dark this game can be in the last episodes, behind the cheery facade there's evidence that this in fact could be the Chronicles of the Darkness world.<br /> <br /> For more thought, Max also seem to have access to some of the Fate Arcana, such as Shifting the Odds (Fate \u2022\u2022) she always seems to find what she needs around her, be it a person, place or thing. She's also exceptionally lucky, as it is evident throughout the game that fortune favors her. As for her Nimbus, you can notice that whenever she uses her powers, the world seem to play in reverse, it doesn't only happen when she uses rewind because in the (spoilers ahead) nightmare sequence of Episode 5 you can see that her powers are symbolized by everything going in reverse (also the nightmare sequence itself can be seen as a second visit to the Supernal Realms)<br /> <br /> /nerd mode off<br /> <br /> So what do you think, Life is Strange fans?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T17:35:29-07:00","id":1152649,"title":"","content":"One more thing, the entire game seem to be themed around Choice and Consequence, what is the Acanthus approach to the Supernal? <i>Choice</i> and <i>Consequence</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theon